ved outputs closely: climb down 239/262 (nb 239), climb up 199-228 (nb 199), jumping 228-250 (nb 250), lying 228 (nb 239), sitting 228-239 (nb 228), standing 488 (nb 488), walking 262-288 (nb 262); running 620-651 vs nb 443 (nb used calc_steps(2000) on 2,024 rows)."},"stopping_point_summary":{"notebook_order_start50":{"median":75.0,"min":60,"max":542,"n_activities":25,"n_never_saturated":0,"frac_in_400_600":0.16},"notebook_order_start100":{"median":383.0,"min":126,"max":683,"n_activities":25,"n_never_saturated":1,"frac_in_400_600":0.33}},"saturation_points_used_in_paper":{"per_activity":{"Bed_making":488,"Cutting_Components":465,"Cycling":465,"Dancing":591,"Drawing":488,"Driving":443,"Eat_with_hand":465,"Flipping":488,"Piano":443,"Playing Guitar":488,"Praying":465,"Put off clothes":465,"Reading":443,"Rowing":488,"Running":465,"Shaking_dust":126,"Sweeping":443,"Typing_on_keybord":512,"Washes_dishes":488,"Washing_Hands":422,"Wearing Clothes":422,"Wiping":620,"Writting_on_Paper":422,"playing violin":488,"shower":563},"median":465.0,"mean":466.2,"min":126,"max":620,"frac_in_400_600":0.92,"source":"size of motion_embedding/t2m-gpt/had-aw_1000_optimal/<act>.npy = number of descriptions kept by the saturation-point algorithm (init 100, +5%/step; which modality drove it, text or motion, is not recorded in the repo - the paper says text); these sets presumably underlie the With Saturation Point rows of tables/algo_eval.tex. Values are all on the calc_steps(.,0.05,100) grid."}}